Package: usb-auth-guard
Version: 1.0.0
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Depends: usbguard, python3, python3-dbus, python3-gi
Recommends: usbguard-dbus, polkitd | policykit-1, kde-cli-tools | zenity
Maintainer: SolVerNA <gizartv@gmail.com>
Homepage: https://github.com/SolVerNA/usb-auth-guard
Description: USB device authorization daemon with polkit password prompt
 Blocks all USB devices by default and shows a native desktop
 password dialog (polkit/KDE/GNOME) before allowing any new device.
 .
 Protects against BadUSB attacks, USB HID injection (Rubber Ducky,
 O.MG Cable), and USB data exfiltration by requiring user authentication
 for every new device insertion.
 .
 Uses USBGuard for low-level USB blocking and polkit for authentication,
 providing the same security model as sudo GUI prompts.
